---
description: better-giving project rule
alwaysApply: true
---

The project facts (stack, commands, boundaries, never-do list) live in `AGENTS.md` at the
repo root. Follow it; don't restate it here. If anything conflicts, `AGENTS.md` wins.

- Before reporting done, run the checks CI runs from the repo root: `pnpm exec biome format .`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm check`, `pnpm test`, and `go test ./...` in `packages/console`. `pnpm test` takes several minutes. `packages/form`'s browser specs are a separate CI job (`pnpm --filter @better-giving/form test:browser` after that package's Playwright Chromium install) and `pnpm test` never reaches them.
- Tests need no production secrets. Don't add a real `packages/app/.dev.vars` or a Cloudflare token to make them pass.
- Ignore `.claude/` unless the task is about agent setup. It's Claude Code / kru config.
- Never print or commit a secret. Never run `pnpm deploy`, `pnpm deploy:test`, or `pnpm deploy:vars`.
